  "body": "Part of #363 (research comment there has the sources and the safety reasoning).\n\nPriority: P2\n\nParams: dip interval (axial, at least N leads), dip height (at most the current pass's depth of cut, along the infeed vector), and dip length.\n- Never on the first approach lead or the last lead; never on the finish or spring passes.\n- New CL segment: a synchronized move with a radius change, plus simulator and verdict support.\n- Posts declare `continuousThreading`. fanuc-lathe G32 emits the dip as `G32 X Z F` segments. G76 and posts without the flag refuse by name.\n\n*Done means:*\n- The primary-source citation for Fanuc continuous thread cutting is recorded in the post header before the code lands.\n- Pinning tests: the dip never goes deeper than the pass depth; the phase (station mod lead) is unchanged across the chain; a dip within the approach or exit length, or on the finish pass, is refused; G76 refuses.\n- Golden G32 output.\n",
